  "body": "Specifically, it breaks down badly for partial interfaces. This was discovered in https://github.com/heycam/webidl/pull/155; see especially the comment thread at https://github.com/heycam/webidl/pull/155#discussion_r76880809.\n\nThe right way to fix this is to make the setup of instances, interface prototype objects, and interface objects more imperative (as is currently done for namespaces).\n\nAlso, it would help if mixins were a first-class concept, instead of something you get when using [NoInterfaceObject] and also only ever using the interface on the right-hand side of an `implements` statement\n",
